 turning oil into a pool of blazing  treacle and lightning causing every  puddle of water into an electrical  hazard every element is hazardous but  combined elements are downright deadly  both to you and the colorful array of  creatures and cultists you face every  battle requires that you proceed with  caution though you could say that about  all of divinity original sin each choice  you make even seemingly minor ones could  result in unforeseen consequences and  it's the natural systematic way in which  of those consequences play out that make  original sin stand out among other RPGs  that also boast multiple parts and moral  quandaries divinity original sin  provides a world of wonder and a fair  challenge using the trappings of the  classics weird or to tell a brand new  tale and to introduce brand new tactical  considerations it is sometimes funny and  sometimes grim sometimes tense and  sometimes easygoing but original sin is  always special and the runaway winner  for july's game in the month award
 

